<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<CustomPermission xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS NOTE LIVES IN A COMMENT, NOT IN <description>, DELIBERATELY.
        CustomPermission.Description is capped at 255 characters (measured 2026-08-12 via
        Acquisition_Deal_Actions.customPermission-meta.xml's own first-draft dry-run failure:
        "Value too long for field: Description maximum length is: 255"). Broker_Protection_Access
        carries the same workaround for the identical reason. A comment is repo-only and is never
        sent to the Metadata API, so it can be as long as it needs.

        PHASE 1 (2026-08-12) of retiring the driver-flag concept — see
        agent-output/design-requirements-custom-permissions.md. This IS the layer-5 AUTHORIZATION
        token for the Disposition deal-action gate, replacing the FLS-on-a-checkbox mechanism
        (User.Disposition_Driver__c). It is granted through Disposition_Deal_Driver.permissionset-
        meta.xml — the same layer-5 set that already carries the fieldPermissions grant on
        User.Disposition_Driver__c, so the population is preserved by construction (same set, same
        holders) rather than by a migration script.

        THIS PHASE REPOINTS THE FLEXIPAGE HALF ONLY. The 6 disposition-gated visibility criteria
        (LOI_Record_Page x3, NDA_Record_Page x2, Contract_Review_Record_Page x1) now read
        {!$Permission.CustomPermission.Disposition_Deal_Actions} instead of
        {!$User.Disposition_Driver__c}. DispositionActionPermissionService.cls still reads the OLD
        flag, unchanged, until the developer agent's parallel pass lands
        FeatureManagement.checkPermission('Disposition_Deal_Actions') — until then the chrome and
        the server-side assert are DELIBERATELY out of sync for the disposition module, exactly as
        they were for acquisitions during the P0 spike window. User.Disposition_Driver__c and its
        fieldPermissions grant on Disposition_Deal_Driver are UNTOUCHED and remain the rollback
        lever; they are retired in a separate, later pass (see the design doc section 6).

        🔴 DO NOT ADD THIS PERMISSION TO A LAYER-4 CAPABILITY SET (e.g. a future
        Disposition_Stage_Actions_Access). ARCHITECTURE.md section 2's seven-layer model states
        layer 4 answers "can this code be reached at all" and layer 5 answers "is this specific
        user allowed" — a custom permission changes the TOKEN, not the QUESTION. Merging it into a
        capability set would grant deal-driving to that set's ENTIRE membership in one deploy,
        exactly the widening Acquisition_Deal_Driver's own comment already warns against for its
        sibling gate.
    -->
    <label>Disposition Deal Actions</label>
    <description>Layer-5 authorization token for the Disposition stage quick actions. Replaces User.Disposition_Driver__c. Grant ONLY via Disposition_Deal_Driver; never via a layer-4 capability set.</description>
    <isLicensed>false</isLicensed>
</CustomPermission>
